        "statement": "Adopt as a physical assumption of this framework: (i) the oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space (A,V,eta,C^+) is the spacetime of the framework; its points represent idealized physical events, displacements represent idealized spacetime separations, and the sign classification of eta is the adopted causal structure; (ii) the equations of the specific mechanical and electromagnetic models developed from this framework are covariant under the affine maps F: A -> A whose linear part L satisfies eta(Lv,Lw) = eta(v,w) for all v,w in V, has determinant +1 relative to the adopted orientation, and maps C^+ onto C^+; such maps are the inertial changes of description. These assumptions are adopted, not deduced from experiment nor from the verbal postulates of Einstein, and they define the framework's scope. Covariance is asserted for the specified model equations only: it does not select a force or matter law, does not forbid explicitly adopted background structure by a purely syntactic test, and carries no claim that the physical world is exactly described by the model.",
